<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71094" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νότ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Pr.</u>
			402
		</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			2.1.22
		</span></i>, etc. :—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>moist, damp, rainy,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. ἱδρώς</span>
			<i>damp</i> sweat, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.811
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				23.715
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. θέρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					107.13
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔαρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Aph.</u>
					3.11
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				860a36
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παγαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
				</span></i>
			 l.c. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑψοῦ δ᾽ ἐν νοτίῳ τήν γ᾽
				ὅρμισαν [ναῦν]</span> well out in <i>the water,</i> opp.
			the beach, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.785
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.55
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. δῖναι ἅλμας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					150
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.) : 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				4.4.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bringing rain,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστέρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arat.
					238
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				490
			</span></i> (both 
				Comp.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to the south, southern,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. θάλασσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.13
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				6.31
			</span></i> ; esp. of the Indian Ocean, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.17
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.11
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				158
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τεῖχος τὸ ν.,</span> at
			Athens, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				3.7
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. ἀήτης</span> a
			<i>south</i> wind, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1538
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νότια</span> (with or without
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνεύματα</span>) <i>southerly</i>
			winds, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				364a19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1290a14
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοτίοις</span>”
				<i>during southerly winds,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HA</u>
					574a1
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νότια πνεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>CP</u>
					1.13.5
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐὰν ᾖ νότια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HP</u>
					4.14.9
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ν. ἀήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mete.</u>
					377b27
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ν. ὕδατα</span>
			<i>southerly</i> rains, ib.<i><span class="en">
				358a28
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. [ὕδωρ]</span> water <i>from
				southern slopes,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HA</u>
				596a28
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. Ἰχθῦς,</span> the
			constellation <i>Piscis Australis,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eudox.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hipparch.
				2.1.21
			</span></i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νότειος Ἰ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PLond.</u>
					1.130.148
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(i/ii A.D.)</span>) : 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Antr.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			 : 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					13.1.68
				</span></i>
			.</div>
